Ticket #4471 combines reports about two different date-handling bugs. The export contains
overlapping rows, so the components below count each report ID once and group reports by
tenant locale, booking form, and channel.

<Callout>
Keep #4471 as the source merge. Track each cause in its own issue, using the report count
shown in the table below.
</Callout>

## What the causes mean

### `parser` · shared date parser

Day-first tenants send dates through the app, email, and booking-v2 form. The shared parser
reads month first, so it can flip the day and month. The `parser` row groups these reports
across all affected tenants.

### `hint` · booking-v3 date hint

The booking-v3 form displays `MM/DD/YYYY` for day-first tenants. People follow that hint,
but the form reads the value using the tenant's locale. This is a separate cause from the
shared parser.

Intake tags are guesses made from the reporter's browser. They do not determine the cause;
the table shows them only as context. The one-day-move notes are symptoms within the
tenant-specific groups, not a third cause.

